Document: Practice Direction 55A – Possession Claims
Part 2 of 2
==================================================
## 11.3 Paragraphs 2.1(2), 2.4, 2.5, 2.5A, 2.6, 4.1, 7.1 and 7.2 do not apply. ## 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (a) reference to the appropriate claim form and particular of claim is to the following forms as appropriate –

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (i) N5 (W) claim for possession of property;

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (ii) N5B (W) claim for possession of property -Accelerated;

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (iii) N121 (W) claim form (Trespassers);

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (iv) N120 (W) Claim Form (Mortgaged residential premises);

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (v) N119 (W) POC (residential possession); and

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (b) reference to the applicable defence form in connection with a Renting Homes possession claim is to Form N11 R (W) defence form (Rented Premises); and

[This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.4 In paragraph 1.5 –] (c) a claim for an extended possession order must be in the relevant claim form listed in paragraph (a) and be accompanied by the notice required under section 65(3)(b) of the 2016 Act. ## 11.5 Paragraph 2.1(4) is to be read as referring only to details about any occupation contract. [This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.5 Paragraph 2.1(4) is to be read as referring only to details about any occupation contract.] 11.6 Paragraph 2.7 has effect that if the claim is a Renting Homes possession claim under section 178 or section 181 of the 2016 Act in relation to an occupation contract which is a prohibited conduct standard contract or introductory standard contract (provided for under section 16 of that Act), the particulars of claim must have attached to them a copy of the notice provided to the contract-holder in accordance with section 173 or section 182 of that Act. [This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.5 Paragraph 2.1(4) is to be read as referring only to details about any occupation contract.] 11.7 In paragraphs 8.1, 8.3 and 8.4 reference to section 89 of the Housing Act 1980 includes reference to section 219 of the 2016 Act. ## 11.8 Paragraph 10.1 has effect as including reference to sections 211(2) and (3) of the 2016 Act. [This Practice Direction supplements Part 55 > 11.8 Paragraph 10.1 has effect as including reference to sections 211(2) and (3) of the 2016 Act.] Updated: Thursday, 1 December 2022
